an art can be a potent storytelling tool  in anime in just a few episodes a series  can deliver some of its hypest plots  complete with or inspiring action and  heroic moments if you look at it and are  just one small part of a big whole but  this small segment has the potential to  make or break a show a poorly executed  art can make the viewer lose interest  and give up on the show entirely the  Shonan universe is full of arcs that do  an exceptional job of telling a story  effectively and compellingly so today to  commemorate this channel reaching the  very important milestone of 600,000  subscribers yes I wanted to do another  very special and personal video for you  yes I'll be picking 10 of my favourite  shounen arcs in anime this is also in  keeping with my policy of picking just  one entry per series okay but on that  note let's get started  [Music]  we kick off this list with bleaches soul  Society Ark this one is a given and  perhaps the reason why bleach reach the  epic heights it did before it's  inglorious fall from grace before it  went off the rails at bleach was the  core kid on the anime block with the  potential to become one of the greatest  shown in shows of all time and the soul  society Ark is where it all started it  gave us unforgettable characters like in  and Meyer II it had incredible battle  sequences think it's ago versus Kenpachi  or Renji versus byakuya and it left us  with the smartest most deceptively  badass villain the soul society arc did  all the heavy lifting setting the stage  for Bleach to do something incredible a  pity it didn't turn out that way though  isn't it but that moment at the end of  the arc when Aizen snaps his geeky  glasses in half and drops his good guy  facade remains a brilliant legacy of  this fallen giant remember the heavens  arena and hunter exam arcs from hunter  hunter  well this entry on the list is from  Takashi's other notable work YuYu  Hakusho  and i feel it far surpasses both of them  the dark tournament saga follows the  protagonist a you skate or a mushy as he  and his friends enter an underworld  contest where they're pitted against  killers and demons spread across 40  episodes it took almost a year to air  when an arc lasts that long  there's a very good chance of it losing  its way that too when it's mostly all  matches and battles but dark tournament  doesn't falter at all on the contrary  for me is the show's best arc the  battles are intense but the pace never  gets too frenetic thanks to some quiet  moments in between the story shows that  use gaze growth and maturity as he's  pushed to his limits both physically as  he faces freakishly strong opponents and  emotionally as he watches his mentor  fall in battle his ground breaking a  muscle popping final bust up against  togoro has all the destructive power of  a good old 90s anime as an added bonus  togoro makes quite the impression as a  multi-layered villain who's so much more  than his awesome crew car and rippling  muscles  [Music]  next is the final arc of Full Metal  Alchemist Brotherhood from the world of  martial arts we move on to a universe  ruled by alchemy by now I'm sure you  know the story of Edward and Alphonse  Elric brothers and alchemists on a  mission to take back what they lost in a  disastrous failed experiment brotherhood  explores some dark themes loss sacrifice  the limits of humanity this is also true  of its final arc the chief attraction of  which is the battles between the  homunculi and the Elric brothers and  their allies the fight between Roy  Mustang and MV is particularly memorable  because it goes beyond the flame  alchemists impressive takedown of the  shape-shifting homunculus this battle  between hero and villain good and evil  explores one of Brotherhood's dark  themes to great effect the theme being  that nothing is completely black and  white at the end of their contest we see  Mustang so consumed by hatred that he's  on the verge of turning into a beast  himself on the other hand every is  resentful longing for the undying human  spirit makes the homunculus a little  human at some level all in all the final  arc has so many great moments from the  last transmutation scene to the epic  final battle if I ever make a top-10 FMA  moments I'm really going to have a hard  time ranking them 7 we have another  tournament arc a very nostalgic one at  that the tune in exam comes in the first  half of Naruto and it's its first big  arc it serves as a test of skill  intelligence leadership battle prowess  and all the other quantities required in  the next crop of ninjas that inhabit  this world the series is known for its  eloquently choreographed fight sequences  and the Chunin exam gives it its first  bragging rights the matches are of the  highest level and highly entertaining as  the young contestants show off their  wildly different skills from shikamaru's  shadow imitation technique to Rock Lee's  taijutsu it serves up some of the best  underdog fights in anime - such as class  clown Naruto surprising the Hyuga  prodigy nage II with a punch to his face  and changing his outlook on life and  destiny or Rock Lee almost getting the  better of a seemingly invincible and  creepy as hell Gaara and making us all  realize that we dig a hard-working guy  in a green jumpsuit moreover this arc  serves as a great introduction for all  the characters who go on to become  central to Naruto storyline teams  the rookie 19 guy Gaara and Orochimaru  let's not forget him as a narc the  Chunin exam is not just a single event  but rather a launchpad for some of the  most important and enduring friendships  rivalries and relationships that make  this anime special  talking about special there's no anime  quite as special as Gintama its first 50  or episodes are pretty much practical  jokes parodies and madcap moment strung  together with a good bit of satire  thrown into but when it's time to get  serious this show gets right down to it  with even lazy odd jobs boss kintoki  turning into the deadly shiroyasha the  farewell Shinsengumi arc is perhaps the  best example of Gintama smooth  transition from goofy to grim I know a  lot of Gintama fans prefer Shogun  assassination arc over this one and  that's that's pretty fair actually  because I feel it's also one of the best  shown in arcs around however my personal  favorite arcing Gintama is the farewell  Shinsengumi arc battles are the  highlight of any serious Gintama arc but  farewell Shinsengumi deals with  weightiest subjects like personal demons  uncomfortable truths and friendships  between enemies the villains are all  highly memorable the sadistic new Shogun  no boo no boo the meme owada gloomy  which replaces the Shinsengumi is the  Shogunate special police force and the  10:00 show in Naraku a shadowy  assassination group that also works for  the government and it introduces us to  su ro the series toughest antagonist  towards the end the emotions really hit  home with the bickering in toki and  Hijikata sharing a last meal Kagura and  Okita fighting one last jewel and of  course the Shinsengumi saying goodbye to  eddo with a promise to come back someday  [Music]  Rurouni Kenshin known to some Western  audiences as samurai X is a classic  shown in show with heavy undertones of  Japanese history this entry is not an  arc from the series but an original  video animation or OVA that serves as a  prologue to it titled trust and betrayal  is the story of how the protagonist  himura kenshin becomes the infamous man  slayer it also reveals how he got his  famous scar both in its imagery and its  story and treatment the OVA has a darker  more brooding tone than the anime series  trust and betrayal doesn't hold back  with this display of violence bloodshed  and gore at the same time there's a  serenity in quiet beauty about it that's  a complete odds with its violent themes  and yet these two halves make a whole  that never feels jarring the battle  scenes make as much sense as the more  mundane moments in Kenshin's life at  home the beautiful background animation  and use of color make these moments  shine even more trust and betrayal is as  much of a journey of a man's descent  into hellish violence as it is a love  story between a man and a woman who were  perhaps never fated to be together if  you haven't watched the OVA I highly  recommend you do even if you haven't  seen the original series yet  [Music]  next we take a look at return to chigan  china from attack on titan no shown and  listing can be complete without an entry  from attack on Titan the show that's  made a habit of upping the anticipation  with each new season  it's the latest arc returned to shegaon  China follows Eren Mikasa and Armin as  they returned to their hometown four  years after it fell to Titans they're  part of an ambitious expedition to learn  the truth behind the Titans and reclaim  war Maria but it's more accurately a  suicide mission  given the waiting for them is a fierce  battle against the beast Titan and  certain death the action is fantastic as  usual Levi's mowing down an army of  Titans and almost killing the Beast  Titans probably the most badass one-man  show in anime but the fights this time  are as emotionally charged as they are  bruising this is especially true of the  clashes between the survey corpsmembers  and the armored and colossal titans the  writing effectively captures the inner  struggles on both sides it does the same  when Levi has given the unenviable task  of choosing one life over another within  the space of just 10 episodes  major characters die a new Titan is born  and an old enemy reveals his hidden  connection to Eren at the end of all  this tragedy and bloodshed the mission  to learn the truth hidden in Aaron's old  basement ends in success but also in  mixed feelings return tsch against  enough for me is attack on titans best  art yet and it raises the bar high for  how the rest of the story will unfold PS  we dig the new Thunder Spears  [Music]  the show posted a classic game of  cat-and-mouse between a serial killer  and an eccentric detective brings up the  rear of our top three shown in arcs the  battle of wits between Light Yagami as  the serial killer Keira and Elle is  legendary and needs no introduction  given Elle's popularity among fans the  animes first 26 episodes is called the a  lark though you could argue in reality  it comprises three arcs the super arc  tells the story of Lights descent into  darkness on finding the Death Note and  meeting the Shinigami ryu k-- Elle's  pursuit of Kira and the battle of  one-upmanship that ensues between the  two what makes this battle a hoot to  watch is the characters of its players  light is a model student on the surface  popular and talented but deep within he  is an evil incarnate a manipulative  killer with a god complex and no remorse  l on the other hand has a slouchy  appearance that makes others doubt his  abilities but he's highly intelligent  meticulous and analytic he's also deeply  suspicious deceptive prone to lying and  not above using cruel and criminal means  to get what he wants the art comes alive  with their scheming and planning as it  is in every battle there's a winner and  a loser this applies to the contest  between light and L as well by now most  of us know how it ends the L arc is not  the end of Death Note but it might as  well be after all I'd say this is when  the series started to go downhill for me  personally but the airlock on its own is  a masterpiece and no one can convince me  otherwise  who  at number two is marineford from  one-piece action adventure ship loads of  cool characters and heartbreak come  together in this arc that one piece fans  will probably never get over as the  Admirals and their allies go up against  the might of the white beard pirates and  Luffy's motley crew the action never  stops for a moment  but these frenetically paced 33 episodes  are more than just the fighting the  marineford arc has some splendidly  written moments such as white bids  fierce last stand and garbs quiet grief  then there shanks who makes one of the  biggest impacts on this arc despite  being absent for the most part of it in  his short cameo we get a glimpse of the  quiet power of this man that we've seen  much too little of so far the marineford  arc takes the viewers through a gamut of  emotions as courage and loyalty clash  with treachery and deceit it will  probably have you hating Blackbeard in a  canoe with a vengeance  not that we blame you for it though of  course but nothing hurts quite as much  as the tragedy that awaits us at the end  in this rollercoaster called one peace  the story of marineford will break your  heart like no tragedy drama ever can  [Music]  what Emily  in the top spot then we have the Chimera  ant Ark from the 2011 anime reboot of  Hunter hunter this shows pretty much the  manual on great story arcs if you've  watched the phantom troop and zoldak  family segments you'll know what I'm  talking about but for me this arc is  undoubtedly the most superior of them  all given the show's track record it  comes as no surprise that the action is  of the highest level in this one maderos  deathmatch with Miriam and guns rage  moment against Pete oh don't have an  equivalent but even in the clashes  between secondary characters the actions  more than skin-deep and crackles with  innovation and personality the hunter's  invasion of maryam's castles more  goosebump inducing than title fights in  some anime in between the fighting there  are moments where the story changes pace  and just breathes a little yet these  moments are just as vital to the  narrative as the boom and bombast of the  fight sequences mara where's shogi game  with kabuki is one such contemplative  sequence while seemingly not part of the  main story it's nevertheless critical to  the change in the ant Kings personality  before he engages the hunter in battle  it gives the ruthless Miriam a  compassionate even human side that we've  never actually seen before it's a  turning point in his evolution as one of  the greatest anime antagonists of all  time the art comes to a  thought-provoking end raising questions  about the concepts of hero and villain  good and evil you gotta watch it to  believe it this arc is the main reason  why Hunter hunter 2011 is still my  favorite anime of all time  and that's the end of this video I hope  you enjoyed watching it if you did give  it a like tell me in the comments below  what's your top 10 shown in arcs in  anime I'd love to hear from you on this  one and do subscribe for more cool anime  content I would like to thank you once  again for helping this channel reach  600,000 subscribers I'm truly grateful I  couldn't have done it without you and  for those of you who haven't subscribed  yet please consider doing it if you  enjoy this type of content and hit the  bell button so that you never miss any  of my uploads stay tuned and I'll see  you next time on Vinny tube  [Music]
 

